# Versioning rules (<% derived.option_labels.versioning %>)

<%#eq options.versioning "nbgv"%>- `version.json` at the repository root is the single version source; bump `version` there for a new minor/major. Patch numbers come from git height; never hand-write build numbers.
- CI reads the version with the `dotnet/nbgv` GitHub Action and tags images with `SemVer2`; `nbgv tag` creates the git tag on the release branch.
- Public releases only from `publicReleaseRefSpec` branches (`main`); other branches produce prerelease versions that must not be deployed beyond `dev`.
<%/eq%><%#eq options.versioning "semantic-release"%>- Commit messages follow Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `test:`; `!` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` for majors). The release version is derived from them; a wrong type produces a wrong version.
- Releases are cut only by the release job on the release branch (`main`); never create tags or GitHub releases by hand.
- The release commit (`chore(release): vX.Y.Z [skip ci]`) is generated; do not amend or rebase over it.
<%/eq%>- One versioning scheme per repository. Switching schemes is a `/adlc:bootstrap` decision, not a workflow edit.
